title: JSON, fingerprints, secrets, and zip files
card: Chapter 14 | JSON | Reaching into what web services send
say:
  Web services answer in JSON: names, values and lists inside each other. The json library reaches straight in, with a path.
uncard

new: weather.stella
type fast:
  use: json

  genesis:
    set answer to replace "~" with a quotation mark in "{~city~: ~Oslo~, ~days~: [{~high~: 4}, {~high~: 7}]}"
    scrawl "City: ", the json at with (answer, "city")
    scrawl "Tomorrow's high: ", the json number at with (answer, "days[2].high")
    scrawl "Days: ", the size of the json list at with (answer, "days")
    set answer to the json changed at with (answer, "days[1].high", "5")
    scrawl answer
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 4-5
spot: line 4
say: Here's an answer like a weather service might send. Each tilde becomes a quote mark, to keep the line easy to read.
spot: line 5
say: The json at, with a path: the part called city.
zoom: lines 6-7
spot: line 6
say:
  Names go with dots between them, and items in square brackets, counted from one. So days, item two, high.
spot: line 7
say: The json list at gives a list, to go through or count.
zoom: lines 8-9
spot: line 8
say: And the json changed at gives the whole thing back, with one part changed.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 14 | Fingerprints and secrets | Hashing and encryption
say:
  A hash is a fingerprint of some text. It's always the same for the same text, and completely different if one letter changes.
  Encryption keeps text secret: only someone with the password can read it.
uncard
new: secret.stella
type fast:
  use: hashing
  use: encryption

  genesis:
    scrawl the hash of with ("sha256", "hello")
    scrawl the hash of with ("sha256", "hellp")
    set secret to encrypted with ("meet at noon", "swordfish")
    scrawl secret
    scrawl decrypted with (secret, "swordfish")
    try:
      scrawl decrypted with (secret, "wrong")
    if that went wrong:
      scrawl "Wrong password: ", the wound
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 5-6
spot: lines 5-6
say: Hello and hellp differ by one letter, but their fingerprints have nothing in common. Websites keep fingerprints of passwords, not the passwords.
zoom: lines 7-9
spot: line 7
say: Encrypted with turns the message into text that can be kept or sent anywhere.
spot: line 9
say: Decrypted with, and the same password, gives it back.
zoom: lines 10-13
spot: lines 10-13
say: A wrong password is a problem. So is any change to the secret text, so changes are always noticed.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 14 | Zip files | Many files in one
uncard
new: backup.stella
type fast:
  use: zip

  genesis:
    inscribe "Level 3, 120 coins" into file "save.txt"
    pack the zip with (a list containing "save.txt", "backup.zip")
    scrawl the files in the zip "backup.zip"
    unpack the zip with ("backup.zip", "restored")
    scrawl contents of file "restored/save.txt"
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 4-8
spot: line 5
say: Pack the zip puts files and folders, with everything inside them, into one zip file.
spot: line 6
say: The files in the zip lists what it holds.
spot: line 7
say: And unpack the zip puts them all into a folder.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out
